    <TD align="left" valign="top" colspan="4" height="115"><b><p>I was born to Cedric and Lissa D’Esiste on a beautiful summer day.  My father was a Deputy and served proudly in the Guardians of Vale forces. My father loved being a deputy. The one thing I can remember about my father to this day is his favorite phrase, “Cease and Desist”.  (Which by the way is how I got my name.)   My mother was your typical stay at home parent. She was very loving and caring, always nurturing me and talking to me about the ways of Rivervale and the lands of Norrath.</p>
<p>One day when I was 3 yrs old, my parents and I went for a picnic in Misty Thicket. (This was when it was safe to picnic.) It started out as your typical bright, sunny afternoon. When all of a sudden from out of their dark sheltered homes the Runnyeye Goblins emerged into the Thicket. My father being the committed and brave deputy at all times tried to push them back into their cave. My mother feared for our safety and ran to get the other deputies from the Vale. But, alas the Goblins were too many and too strong, my father was killed protecting our beloved Vale, and my mother was killed protecting me. I survived only because my mother found a hollow tree in which she hid me.</p>
<p>After the long hard battle between the Guardians of Vale and the goblins had died down. The goblins were pushed back temporarily into their cave. The deputies began their search for me, knowing they had found my parents twisted corpses they knew I was with them somewhere. The search ended 2 days later as one of the townsfolk heard my cries of hunger and thirst. The kind woman took me home to nourish and bathe me. Since I had no next of kin this kind and wonderful woman offered to take me into their home and raise me with her only daughter. That is how I came to have a sister and new family. I was adopted by the Ondahedd family and looked up to my new sister Boppitt.</p>
<p>All through my childhood I vowed I would get revenge on the Runnyeye goblins that took my parents away from me. I studied hard, and trained secretly with my sister to become a great Warrior. When the time came I went to see Sheriff Roglio and asked to become a member of the Guardians of Vale. He told me I had much training still to do and needed to prove myself worthy. So I began my training, I trained in such things as taunting, weaponry usage, dodging, bashing, parrying, dual wielding and most importantly how to master the double attacks. I began my hunting in the Thicket, now occupied by lookout camps of goblins and the new foes the Deathfist Orcs. To prove my worthiness to the Guardians I was told to collect and turn in Goblin War Beads and Deathfist Orc Belts. It took a lot of hard work and dedication to hunt these foes. But, alas one day after turning in my many packs of belts and beads I went to see Marshall Ghobber. I asked him “Am I one with the Wall?” and to my surprise he said, “YES, and welcome Deputy Ceissa.” Now that I had proven myself it was time to move on and see the vast lands of Norrath and do justice for all the wrongs that have been committed by my foes.</p>
<p>As I was out adventuring, I ran into my sister and best friend Boppitt. She told me of the wonderful group of people she had met. She told me how she had become A Warrior of Wrath. This group sounded adventurous, committed and fun. I then set my goals on becoming one of them.</p>
<p>As fate would have it as I was out ridding the Oasis of those nasty Orcs. I ran into a Magician by the name of Luthir, who happened to belong to the Warriors of Wrath. I talked with him about this group, what their goals were, what type of people belonged, and other details of themselves. During our hunt, this kind magician asked me if I would like to become one of them. Of course there was no hesitation in my response, I said “YES”.</p>
<p>Since that time I have met and hunted with many of the members of this group. I still have yet to find my sister and thank her for her wonderful stories, advice and training. But I know that one day our paths will cross again and hopefully we can fight side by side to take my revenge on those goblins of the Clan Runnyeye.  Until that day comes, I will continue my journeys through the lands of Norrath. And soon I will go adventuring in the newly discovered land of Kunark, for I hear of a new clan of goblins that have taken up residence there. ALL GOBLINS MUST DIE!!!</p>
</b></TD>
